      "note": "Approved on the rule's own verdict, no --override.\n\nEvidence: 5 blocking findings, unowned_blocking 0, verify_later empty (no\nfail-open owner), reviewed_spec_hash == spec_hash, drift []. Linter 0 errors.\nRed-first ok with dynamic.ran true, 21/21 tests red, vacuous_tests [], every\nfixture resolves. 21 criteria, 21 tests, 1:1 coverage. E113 satisfied (setup\nsession 3 cuts vs 4/4/4/5); W114 clear (largest cut share 0.33 vs 0.45).\n\nThe 5 blocking findings are unit/semantics ambiguities and the tests have\nalready fixed a reading: budget in raw cents, apply-plan takes no body and\nreads persisted budgetCents, plan allocates single shares. The Builder\nconverges on the tests.\n\nW112 on all five sessions (44.5 / 43 / 43 / 46.2 / 49.0) accepted deliberately.\nThis is not the W114 \"one oversized cut\" shape that caused the five previous\noverruns - every cut is a flat 6.0 min with 0 stated decisions and hints of\n9-28 words. Per blockers_round_3.md the weighted model scored +5.1 against a\nreal measurement (said 52.1, Pack Writer 48, measured 47), so these estimates\nare expected to run high. Re-read at step 9 and confirm at the step 13 dry run.\n\nNOTE 1 - A2 is only nominally owned. The target-weight percent-vs-fraction\nambiguity is assigned to test-runner, but test_ui_edit_recompute.py reads the\ncurrent input value, adds 0.05, clamps to [0.01, 0.99] and asserts only that\nshares changed - it passes under either reading. Builder: treat target inputs\nas a fraction 0..1.\n\nNOTE 2 - c-3-3 asserts plan[0] only, not the whole sequence, and the seed is\nnot pinned in the spec. Confirm cut-plan-rank is genuinely graded by reading\nmutation.json at step 8 rather than assuming it.\n\nNOTE 3 - the session 5 apply tests mutate shared DB state (PUT /api/targets\nthen POST /api/apply-plan; c-5-4 asserts after < before on average drift). If\nthey go red in ways unrelated to the Builder's code, suspect test order before\nburning retries on the Builder.\n",
